# CS Roman: ห้ามแก้ผลปริวรรต / โรมันฉบับพิมพ์ใน segments

Canonical policy: `books/cs-roman/docs/transliteration_policy.md`

## When the task is Roman spelling, punctuation, editorial note, false bold, or Thai-from-Roman wrong because Roman is wrong

Edit **`books/cs-roman/shared/transforms.json`** only. Run `scan_transform_hits.py` before editing; pin `when.loci` when the same token is correct elsewhere.

## Forbidden (publication / transliteration text)

- Hand-editing `books/cs-roman/output/*.segments.json` for Roman, Thai body text, or publication punctuation
- Hand-editing `books/cs-roman/volumes/*/data/segments.json` for the same purpose
- Patching `text[].value` or `runs` in segments to “fix transliteration” or “fix publication Roman”
- Treating `output/` as the git source of truth for book text

## Allowed elsewhere

- `shared/transforms.json` — publication rules (applied at TeX generate to body / gāthā / hanging; not edition `notes` / `symbol_notes`)
- `volumes/<id>/data/layout.json` — print rhythm (not spelling)
- `shared/style/` — TeX macros (not generated body TeX)
- `shared/sandhi_breaks_overrides.json` — line-break sandhi
- Extract + test + `pipeline.ps1` — recurring PDF extract bugs
- Registered `fixup_*.py` — legacy JSON structure (see `fixup_process.md`), not per-word publication spelling

## Verify

`run_tests.ps1 -Module test_cs_roman_transforms` then `build.ps1 -Volume … -Mode printing`. PDF after generate is the acceptance criterion; `segments.json` may still show pre-transform text.
